    "difficulty": "Challenge",
    "questionText": "A function is defined by \\(f(x) = 4 - 2\\csc\\!\\left(x + \\tfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\). (a) Find the range of \\(f\\), justifying each transformation. (b) State the smallest positive value of \\(x\\) at which \\(f\\) attains its least value on the upper branch \\(y \\ge 6\\), giving the corresponding value of \\(f\\).",
    "marks": 6,
    "examStyle": true,
    "yearCreated": 2026,
