    "questionText": "The curve \\(C\\) has equation \\(y = 2\\,\\csc x + 3\\). (a) By considering the range of \\(2\\,\\csc x + 3\\), determine whether \\(C\\) can cross the \\(x\\)-axis. (b) Hence find the exact number of zeros of \\(C\\) in the interval \\([0, 2\\pi]\\), and give each zero to \\(3\\) decimal places. (c) State, with a reason, why \\(C\\) has no zeros in the interval \\((0, \\pi)\\).",
