    "questionText": "A function is defined by \\(f(x) = 3 - 2\\,\\csc\\!\\left(x - \\tfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\). (a) Find the range of \\(f\\), giving your answer as inequalities in \\(y\\). (b) State the equations of all asymptotes of \\(y=f(x)\\) in the interval \\(0 \\le x \\le 2\\pi\\). (c) Explain why the equation \\(f(x)=3\\) has no solutions.",
    "marks": 6,
    "examStyle": true,
