    "difficulty": "Challenge",
    "questionText": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = 2 + 3\\cot x\\) for \\(0 < x < \\tfrac{\\pi}{2}\\). (a) Determine the range of \\(f\\) on this interval, justifying your answer from the behaviour of \\(\\cot x\\). (b) Hence find the complete set of values of the constant \\(k\\) for which the equation \\(2 + 3\\cot x = k\\) has a solution in \\(0 < x < \\tfrac{\\pi}{2}\\).",
    "marks": 6,
    "examStyle": true,
    "yearCreated": 2026,
